// entity 109 (REMOVED 2026-07-07, user): the leftover "Vault Overload" trigger_use
// (acc_overload_terminal) was deleted - it sat unused in the middle of the Vault. The side
// event is retired: its acc_overload_point struct (was entity 112) and the
// acc_events_overload::init() call in _acc_main are removed too. Non-rendering trigger brush,
// so the LED bake is unaffected; a full build is still run to regenerate the BSP.
// entity 110
// RE-HOMED ONTO THE LIVE POWER SWITCH x[735,799] y[1950,2014] -> x[-761,-697] y[2218,2282] (2026-07-15).
// _acc_emergency_drop's header says "We piggyback on the same triggers placed for power activation", but
// the switch prefab MOVED (add_power_switches.js, 2026-06-18: "relocate the existing corp power_switch
// prefab out of the trench it now floats [in]") and this trigger did not follow - it stayed at the spot
// gen_interactives.js emitted ("beside corp switch"), which the corp trench later turned into open air
// over the east stairs (treads top out at z=-100..-140; nothing solid at z=0). It was ALSO the only LIVE
// emergency trigger: roll_power_switch_side() is hardcoded "corp", so _acc_map_randomizer's
// disable_dead_side_emergency_triggers() triggerenable(false)s the acc_power_vault copy every single run
// -> the 3-shard clutch button was uncallable in any run. New footprint is built around the switch's own
// stock use trigger: prefab _prefabs/acc/power_switch_ww2.map places use_elec_switch at LOCAL
// x[-8,9] y[-24,-5] z[38,60]; at origin (-752,2250,1) with angles "0 90 0" (yaw 90 -> (x,y)=(-ly,lx))
// that solves to WORLD x[-747,-728] y[2242,2259] z[39,61], i.e. a breaker on the east face of the west
// wall (x[-781,-761]). So a player using the switch stands about x[-761,-713] y[2227,2274] on the z=0
// floor - this 64x64x96 box (the generator's useTrigger size) covers exactly that. Probed: floor slab
// x[-781,819] y[2173,2748] z[-96,0] is solid across the whole footprint (bottom face flush at z=0 = the
// same convention as the live acc_cyberware_kiosk), the footprint sits INSIDE the corp_zone player_volume
// z[-16,400] (unlike the trench, which is below it), and it stops at x=-761 so it never overlaps the wall.
// !! PROMPT CONFLICT - THIS BOX FULLY CONTAINS THE STOCK SWITCH'S use_elec_switch ON ALL 3 AXES.
// An earlier version of this comment claimed there was no conflict "because emergency_loop is gated on
// flag power_on". THAT REASONING IS WRONG and it nearly shipped an unwinnable map: emergency_loop gates
// the ACTION (it checks the flag AFTER waittill("trigger")), but a trigger_use PROMPTS from map load no
// matter what its thread does with the notify. Pre-power there are two overlapping trigger_use ents on
// the breaker; if the engine picks ours, [F] fires our notify, we no-op (power is off), and THE POWER CAN
// NEVER BE TURNED ON. The real guard is script-side and lives in _acc_emergency_drop::emergency_prompt_gate
// (triggerenable(false) until the "power_on" flag, live-side only). Keep that gate if you move this box.
// It is only the PRE-power window that conflicts: stock _zm_power::electric_switch delete()s
// use_elec_switch on power-on (our prefab's trigger has no script_noteworthy "allow_power_off").
